#==============================================================================================
#
#   render - A spectral GPU path tracer
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       luce-render turns a luce-geocore GeometrySet (meshes, instances, and the scene
#       component's cameras and lights) into GPU buffers and traces it with compute
#       kernels on luce-gpu. There is no CPU renderer: the host only compiles the scene
#       and records passes. See docs/DESIGN.md.
#
#       Fragments, in ORDER:
#
#       module.lucb    imports and error codes
#       scene.lucb     CompiledScene: world-space triangles, faces and scene objects
#       bvh.lucb       a binned-SAH BVH over boxes (triangles, splats), in the kernels' node layout
#       splats.lucb    Gaussian splat clouds packed for ray tracing (3DGRT), with their BVH
#       camera.lucb    a camera's primary-ray frame for a resolution
#       device.lucb    GpuScene, the scene's buffers, and the primary-ray probe
#       spectrum.lucb  color matching, spectral fits of colors, blackbodies, film matrix
#       environment.lucb  a dome light's image, read and prepared for sampling by importance
#       shader_graph.lucb  materials' node graphs compiled into programs for the kernels
#       textures.lucb  materials' textures (PNG, JPEG, OpenEXR) and programs
#       lights.lucb    UsdLux lights packed for the kernels
#       materials.lucb OpenPBR Surface parameters packed for the kernels
#       light_tree.lucb the light tree over lights and emissive triangles
#       integrator.lucb  Renderer: the wavefront path tracer's passes
#       loading.lucb   what a renderer loads besides geometry: lights, materials, constants, kernels
#       session.lucb   RenderSession: a progressive render a Luce application shows
#       kernels.lucb   the GLSL kernels, embedded (tools/build_kernels.py; do not edit)
#       tests.lucb     tests of the host side
#
#==============================================================================================

